tomlc17: allow opt-in per-parse duplicate assignment handling

DENG-509 needs warning-only duplicate localization strings without changing strict
ordinary TOML parsing or process-global options. A callback can retain the first
assignment after the replacement is fully parsed. Table headers and inline table
entries stay strict. Allocator and callback context are isolated per parse.

Engine-local extension; remove if an upstream per-parse policy supersedes it.

